CONCLUSION (see ATTEMPT.md sec 7 for the full discussion):
Every piece of T(L)'s r-sum is a genuine, verified, terminating
hypergeometric SERIES in r -- it therefore trivially equals a
terminating 3F2(...) hypergeometric FUNCTION value, a legitimate
'closed form involving a special function' per the mandate's own
named fallback outcome. But Gosper's algorithm PROVES it has no
hypergeometric-term antidifference (elementary Gamma-ratio form),
and sp.hyperexpand independently fails to reduce the 3F2 to an
elementary expression for symbolic K,n -- so the obstruction is
REAL, PRECISELY LOCATED (in this specific r-summation step, one
level up from the predecessor's own subset-sum term-count growth),
and certified by two independent algorithms, not merely 'sympy
gave up'.
